            <ArticleTitle>Leiomyosarcoma of the duodenum in two horses.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>119-23</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Two horses affected by chronic, intermittent colic were found, at post-mortem examination, to have localized annular thickening of a segment of the duodenum. Histological examination of the lesion in both cases revealed a tumour composed of bundles of oval or spindle-shaped cells that stained as muscle with van Gieson stain. The histological diagnosis was leiomyosarcoma. The tumour had caused partial bowel obstruction in both horses.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
